@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ Receive loop (main.py:1496-2516):
 - `type` and `payload` (default `{}`) are read from the message. Unknown types are ignored with no reply.
 - Since 2026-10-10 `ping` (no payload) is answered with `pong` at once, before anything else is read. It is the desk's heartbeat: after 10 seconds with nothing heard the desk pings, and a ping with no answer (`pong` or any other frame) within 15 seconds (so about 30 seconds at most, before the server's own 40) means the socket is dead though it looks open, so the desk opens a new one. Chromium keeps a socket open through a network that goes quiet, and a mark sent into it was lost (playtest, `offline-not-shown`). The desk also shows the banner and reconnects at once on the browser's `offline` event. Since 2026-10-11 a mark the desk sent with no answer yet goes again on the new socket with its `mark_id` (see `take_mark`), drawn held meanwhile; it was let go when the heartbeat replaced the socket, and lost without a word (playtest 2, `silent-socket-loses-mark`).
 - Target character for the message: `payload.character_id` when present, otherwise `int(game_id)` when the path is numeric, otherwise None. The `character` variable is reassigned on every message. Any message carrying a `character_id` therefore acts on that character, whichever socket sent it.
